      "abstained": false,
      "answer": "For a patient with measles, healthcare personnel should use respiratory protection at least as protective as a fit-tested, NIOSH-certified N95 respirator upon entry into the patient's room or care area, regardless of presumptive evidence of immunity. Susceptible healthcare personnel should not enter the room if immune care providers are available. Although Airborne Precautions are recommended for preventing airborne transmission of measles and varicella-zoster viruses, there are no data upon which to base a recommendation for respiratory protection to protect susceptible personnel against these two infections.",
      "citations": [
        "cdc-isolation-precautions-2007#recommendations-for-measles-in-healthcare-settings-p-108-0",
