      "abstained": false,
      "answer": "Hand washing with soap and water is the preferred means when exposure to potential spore-forming pathogens is strongly suspected or proven, including outbreaks of C. difficile (IB). For C. difficile, handwashing with soap and water is preferred because of the absence of sporicidal activity of alcohol in waterless antiseptic handrubs. During C. difficile-associated outbreaks, handwashing with a plain or antimicrobial soap and water is recommended following glove removal after caring for patients with diarrhoea.",
